<ProjectLayout slug="vis-a-vis-verification">
  <p>
    <em>vis-a-vis verification</em> is a video installation
    exploring reflection, repetition, bodily presence and the
    unstable relationship between an image and its counterpart.
  </p>

  <p>
    Through mirrored movements and fragmented visual sequences, the
    work examines how recognition is produced between two opposing
    images and how that recognition can gradually become uncertain.
  </p>

